# Lab 9 – Ensemble Methods with Random Forest

## Objective

The objective of this lab was to learn how ensemble methods improve machine learning performance by combining the predictions of multiple models. I compared the performance of a single Decision Tree with a Random Forest classifier and explored how feature importance can be used to better understand a model.

## What I Did

In this lab, I trained a **Decision Tree Classifier** and a **Random Forest Classifier** using the Iris dataset. I compared the accuracy of both models to see how ensemble learning can improve prediction performance. I also extracted and visualized feature importance scores from the Random Forest model to identify which flower characteristics contributed most to accurate classifications.

## What I Learned

This lab demonstrated that combining multiple models can often produce more accurate and reliable predictions than relying on a single model. I learned how Random Forest reduces overfitting by combining many decision trees and how feature importance helps explain which variables have the greatest impact on a model's decisions.

